<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Configuration>

  <!--
    The manual acceptance sandbox for a packaged Papyrus install.

    ## Why this exists beside the gate

    `papyrus.wsb` runs `run-in-sandbox.ps1`, which copies `build/install` and tests it. That proves the
    install tree, and it never runs the installer. This configuration runs the real
    `Papyrus-1.5.0-setup.exe` from `build/dist`, and a person installs it, registers, adds a source,
    searches, and reads a chapter. The screenshot watcher records what appeared.

    This is manual acceptance evidence. It does not become a gate pass, because a person clicking
    through a flow is not reproducible in the way the gate is.

    ## Why the installer is copied to the desktop

    The mapped installer folder is read only, and running a setup executable from a mapped folder is
    not how a reader meets one. `manual-sandbox.ps1` copies the executable to the desktop, verifies
    its size and SHA-256 against `expected-installer.txt`, and points the shortcut at the copy.

    ## The results folder

    The host creates a fresh `build/manual-sandbox-results/session-<timestamp>` folder before this is
    launched, writes the expected installer hash into it, and maps it to `C:\results`. A missing
    host folder is never created by Windows Sandbox: the mount fails, the logon command never runs,
    and the window closes looking like a slow boot.

    ## The screenshot loop

    `capture-screen.ps1` starts hidden and writes a PNG every ten seconds to `C:\results`. The
    `Stop screenshots` desktop shortcut writes `STOP.txt`, which ends it cleanly. The named step
    capture is separate, so the loop is the record and the named frames are the index.

    ## One guest at a time

    Windows Sandbox refuses a second guest while one is open, and it can do that by exiting zero with
    no message. The host launcher checks for a running guest before it starts this.
  -->

  <VGpu>Disable</VGpu>
  <Networking>Default</Networking>

  <MappedFolders>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>%PAPYRUS_REPO_ROOT%\build\dist</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\installer</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>true</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>%PAPYRUS_REPO_ROOT%\build\sandbox</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\sandbox</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>true</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>%PAPYRUS_MANUAL_RESULTS%</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\results</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>false</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
  </MappedFolders>

  <LogonCommand>
    <Command>powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\sandbox\manual-sandbox.ps1</Command>
  </LogonCommand>

</Configuration>
